COMMAND "Add a Plugin-Declared Schema Type" DESCRIPTION "Scaffold a new plugin-declared document type in the MINIMAL-template shape (charter D54c/D59): create the plugin's bundled schema JSON (name/title/icon/visibility/fields — one sample field, NO dataset key, NO type key) and wire it into the plugin module's register_schemas/1 as a second byte-identical 6-key SchemaDefinition wrap, exactly the scaffy/bulldocs/sheets shape. Visibility is a ONEOF enum variable (D56): the engine refuses any --var Visibility outside public|private at substitution time, before anything is written. Bootstrap auto-registers the result on every boot, idempotent on (name, dataset)." LAST_UPDATED "17-07-2026-00-00-00" DOMAIN "barkpark" TAGS "plugin", "schema" CONCEPT "schema-type" VARIANT "minimal-template" DIRECTION "add" VARIABLES
  VARIABLE 1 "Plugin" TITLE "The target plugin (minimal-template shape)" DESCRIPTION "Lowercase plugin name, referenced as {{.plugin}} in both target paths: the module file api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex and the bundled schemas dir api/priv/plugins/{{.plugin}}/schemas/. Must be one of the MINIMAL-template plugins (scaffy, bulldocs, sheets — see the scope prose below): the wiring anchors are byte-exact against that shared shape, and any other plugin fails loud at anchor resolution. The module file must already exist — the engine's typed PathMissingError enforces that precondition for free (exit 4, nothing written)." EXAMPLES "scaffy", "bulldocs", "sheets"
  VARIABLE 2 "SchemaName" TITLE "The document type name" DESCRIPTION "The new type's name, in two spellings-as-transforms: {{.schema-name}} (the JSON `name` value, the bundled filename, the mark suffixes) and {{.schema_name}} (the `raw_` Elixir variable suffix inside register_schemas/1). Lowercase; the persisted `_type` discriminator documents queries forever, so pick it like an API name." EXAMPLES "release-note", "changelog"
  VARIABLE 3 "Title" OPAQUE TITLE "Human title for the Studio desk" DESCRIPTION "The plural human label the Studio shows for the type (the `title` JSON key). OPAQUE: emitted verbatim — it may carry spaces and capitals that must never be re-cased. This file spells it {{.Title}} exactly once." EXAMPLES "Release Notes", "Changelogs"
  VARIABLE 4 "Icon" OPAQUE TITLE "Desk icon (emoji)" DESCRIPTION "The `icon` JSON value — an emoji, matching the minimal-template precedent (command.json ships one). OPAQUE verbatim literal, spelled {{.Icon}} exactly once; never re-cased, never interpreted." EXAMPLES "🧾", "📓"
  VARIABLE 5 "Visibility" ONEOF "public", "private" TITLE "Anonymous-read visibility" DESCRIPTION "The schema's `visibility` — public gives tokenless reads on the generic query endpoint (the scaffy/bulldocs choice), private returns 404 anonymously and requires a token (the sheets choice). ONEOF is the runtime wall (D56): any other value is a usage error at substitution — exit 2, nothing written. Referenced in its lowercase spelling {{.visibility}} in both the JSON value and the Elixir wrap's Map.get default." EXAMPLES "public", "private"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT THIS COMMAND HONESTLY DOES — and what it deliberately does NOT
#
#   ● api/priv/plugins/{{.plugin}}/schemas/{{.schema-name}}.json  created
#   ○ api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex                     injected ×2 —
#     a raw_{{.schema_name}} read pipeline + a second %SchemaDefinition{} wrap
#
# SCOPE = the MINIMAL template ONLY: the byte-identical 6-key wrap the scaffy /
# bulldocs / sheets plugins share (scaffy.ex:61-78 is the exemplar; bulldocs.ex
# :141-158 and sheets.ex:109-126 carry the same bytes, differing only in the
# JSON filename and sheets' "private" Map.get default). OUT OF SCOPE, BY NAME:
#
#   * frt / media — the EXTENDED 10-key shape: SchemaDefinition.parse/2
#     round-trips (frt.ex:147, media.ex:99) plus desk placement keys. CAMELCASE
#     TRAP, only in THIS out-of-scope shape: the JSON spells `deskGroups`, the
#     Elixir struct field is `desk_groups` (frt.ex:126, media.ex:108,
#     schema_definition.ex:24) — a rename this command never touches.
#   * onixedit — the sub-schema splice: one schema assembled from split JSON
#     parts, not one file per type.
#   * tickets / quiz — the INLINE-Elixir style: the SchemaDefinition is built
#     in code (quiz.ex:96-104 via Content.schema/0, tickets.ex:82) with NO
#     bundled JSON to anchor on.
#
# ADJACENT PRIOR ART, different artifact half: `bp make schema <name>`
# (internal/cli/make_cmd.go) emits a schema v2 JSON skeleton for hand-POSTing
# to /v1/schemas — the AD-HOC registration path (admin auth, tenant stamped
# from the request). This command owns the OTHER half: PLUGIN-DECLARED schemas,
# bundled in priv/ and re-registered by Bootstrap on every boot. D10's "overlaps
# bp make schema" is stale for exactly this reason.
#
# PRECONDITION, enforced FREE: both IN-ops target the plugin module file, so a
# plugin that does not exist (or a typo'd {{.plugin}}) dies as the engine's
# typed PathMissingError — exit 4, nothing written — before any anchor logic.
#
# MANUAL STEPS (prose, deliberately not blind ops):
#
# 1. The plugin's CONTRACT TEST pins the one-schema shape — e.g. scaffy_test.exs
#    setup asserts `[%SchemaDefinition{} = def] = Scaffy.register_schemas([])`,
#    a ONE-element list match that reds the moment this wrap lands. Extend that
#    pin to the two-element list (and cover the new type) in the same change;
#    the TIER ci gate below is what proves you did.
# 2. The plugin MANIFEST lists its schemas descriptively — plugin.json's
#    `schemas` array (e.g. priv/plugins/scaffy/plugin.json), which the same
#    contract test exact-matches. Add the {"name", "version", "file"} row there
#    when you extend the test.
#
# GUARDS: both IN-op payloads plant a `scaffy:add-schema-type … MARK:…` comment
# (D3c — the mark line is the re-run check). The wrap op is a SELF-CONSUMING
# REPLACE (the re-emitted tail survives inside its own payload), so E-005
# requires its payload-derived ASLONG + REANCHOR pair. RE-RUN MATRIX: same
# schema re-run → guards skip both ops (idempotent); a SECOND schema on the
# same plugin → the read op inserts after the same anchor, and the wrap op's
# REANCHOR splice accretes at the mark-family tail (the proven add-cli-verb
# idiom: prior wrap gains the separator comma, the new wrap lands after it,
# the list closer stays untouched).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Op 1: the bundled schema JSON ────────────────────────────────────────────

# The minimal-template key set, mirroring command.json's field style: name /
# title / icon / visibility / fields with ONE sample body field. NO `dataset`
# key (the wrap hardcodes "production", the minimal-template law) and NO `type`
# key (the schema's `name` IS the document type discriminator).
CREATE FILE IF ABSENT "api/priv/plugins/{{.plugin}}/schemas/{{.schema-name}}.json"
WITH
::: {{.schema-name}} schema json :::
{
  "name": "{{.schema-name}}",
  "title": "{{.Title}}",
  "icon": "{{.Icon}}",
  "visibility": "{{.visibility}}",
  "fields": [
    { "name": "title", "title": "Title", "type": "string", "surface": "body" }
  ]
}
::: {{.schema-name}} schema json :::

# ── Op 2: the raw_{{.schema_name}} read pipeline ─────────────────────────────

# Anchor = the existing read pipeline's closing line (unique in every
# minimal-template plugin file: scaffy.ex:66, bulldocs.ex:146, sheets.ex:114 —
# grep -cF = 1 each). The payload inserts a blank separator + the provenance
# mark + a second read of the new bundled JSON through the SAME @schemas_dir
# the plugin already resolves. On a SECOND schema for the same plugin the
# anchor is still the FIRST (original) decode line, so read pipelines stack
# deterministically between it and the list literal. Guard derives from the
# payload (the assignment head this op writes), add polarity (E-011).
IN "api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex"
### Read {{.schema-name}}.json beside the plugin's existing schema read
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: existing read pipeline tail :::
      |> Jason.decode!()
::: existing read pipeline tail :::
WITH
::: {{.schema-name}} read pipeline :::

    # scaffy:add-schema-type {{.plugin}} {{.schema-name}} MARK:schema-read-{{.schema-name}}
    raw_{{.schema_name}} =
      @schemas_dir
      |> Path.join("{{.schema-name}}.json")
      |> File.read!()
      |> Jason.decode!()
::: {{.schema-name}} read pipeline :::
MARK "schema-read-{{.schema-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "raw_{{.schema_name}} ="

# ── Op 3: the second %SchemaDefinition{} wrap ────────────────────────────────

# The proven tail-accretion idiom (add-cli-verb): REPLACE the existing wrap's
# closing tail — its LAST three lines, byte-identical across all three
# minimal-template plugins (fields + dataset + bare `}`; grep-proven exactly
# once per file, the visibility line above them is what differs and is
# deliberately NOT in the anchor) — re-emitting it verbatim WITH the separator
# comma, then the mark + the new 6-key wrap reading raw_{{.schema_name}}. The
# new wrap's Map.get default is {{.visibility}}, so wrap and JSON can never
# disagree. The tail survives inside the payload (self-consuming, E-005), so
# idempotency rests on the payload-derived ASLONG, and REANCHOR keys the
# schema-wrap- mark family: a third schema splices at the family tail (prior
# wrap's bare `}` gains the comma — the D33 tail-shape the template ends in).
IN "api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex"
### Wire {{.schema-name}} as a second SchemaDefinition in register_schemas/1
REPLACE
::: existing wrap tail :::
        fields: Map.get(raw, "fields", []),
        dataset: "production"
      }
::: existing wrap tail :::
WITH
::: existing wrap tail plus {{.schema-name}} wrap :::
        fields: Map.get(raw, "fields", []),
        dataset: "production"
      },
      # scaffy:add-schema-type {{.plugin}} {{.schema-name}} MARK:schema-wrap-{{.schema-name}}
      %SchemaDefinition{
        name: Map.fetch!(raw_{{.schema_name}}, "name"),
        title: Map.get(raw_{{.schema_name}}, "title"),
        icon: Map.get(raw_{{.schema_name}}, "icon"),
        visibility: Map.get(raw_{{.schema_name}}, "visibility", "{{.visibility}}"),
        fields: Map.get(raw_{{.schema_name}}, "fields", []),
        dataset: "production"
      }
::: existing wrap tail plus {{.schema-name}} wrap :::
MARK "schema-wrap-{{.schema-name}}"
REANCHOR "schema-wrap-"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "Map.fetch!(raw_{{.schema_name}}, \"name\")"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POSTCONDITIONS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The bundled JSON exists and carries the chosen visibility verbatim.
ASSERT FILE "api/priv/plugins/{{.plugin}}/schemas/{{.schema-name}}.json" EXISTS
ASSERT FILE "api/priv/plugins/{{.plugin}}/schemas/{{.schema-name}}.json" CONTAINS "\"visibility\": \"{{.visibility}}\""

# Both wiring marks landed, and the wrap actually reads the new raw variable.
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:schema-read-{{.schema-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:schema-wrap-{{.schema-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/plugins/{{.plugin}}.ex" CONTAINS "Path.join(\"{{.schema-name}}.json\")"

# LOCAL: the created file is real JSON (cheap, dependency-light, litter-immune).
ASSERT CMD "python3 -c 'import json; json.load(open(\"api/priv/plugins/{{.plugin}}/schemas/{{.schema-name}}.json\"))'"

# TIER ci: the plugin contract suite — reds until manual step 1 (the one-element
# test pin) and step 2 (the manifest row) land with this scaffold, which is
# exactly the pairing this gate exists to prove. Elixir suites are not on the
# proven local-safe list (fresh worktrees carry no _build).
ASSERT CMD "cd api && mix test test/barkpark/plugins" TIER ci
